# Local runtime/build artifacts (do not commit)
#
# .claude/ is ignored by default, with the review system carved back out. It
# has to travel: untracked files do not copy into a new worktree, so an ignored
# hook simply does not exist there and the Stop check silently never runs.
#
# settings.json is tracked because it is what wires the hook up -- the script
# without its declaration is inert. It holds hook declarations only.
# settings.local.json stays ignored: it holds this machine's permissions.
.claude/*
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/review/
!.claude/settings.json

# Review runtime markers. The ledgers and control patches beside them are
# tracked on purpose; these two are per-run state and would dirty the tree
# mid-review, or be swept into a commit by a broad `git add .review/`.
.review/active
.review/.attempts
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/.vite/
**/dist/
backend/dump.rdb
frontend/storybook-static/

# Local environment files can contain deployment credentials. Keep templates
# such as .env.example and monitoring/.env.example tracked instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!monitoring/.env.example

# Compiled one-off CLI binaries built from backend/cmd
backend/omnichat_prompt_preview

# Local generated / non-product artifacts
.git-lfs/
.superpowers/
.opencode/
opencode.json
TMP_MAIN_STAGE_TEST.glb
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/test-results/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Per-worktree local configuration: each worktree describes its own role,
# so a tracked copy would overwrite every other worktree with one of them.
tasks.json
